STDLIB.md §3, DECISIONS 299, TYPES.md §8.1: E.members holds retired members, and computing with
them is allowed (names, a filter, a String built from all of them are stored fine); a stored value
that still holds a retired member is E3506, as a written one is.
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// E.
enum E { a, retired b, c }

/// All.
let all: [E] = E.members

/// Live.
let live: [E] = E.members.filter(m => not m.retired)

/// Names.
let names: String = E.members.map(.name).join(",")
-- findings.txt --
error[E3506]  a/a.canon:8:16
  all[1]: E.b is retired
  expected by a/a.canon:5 (retired b)

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
